To generate the assert statement for the given comment, we need to ensure that for every index from 0 up to, but not including, the specified index, the element at that position remains unchanged from its previous state, unless it was initially null.

Given the rules and tips, the assert statement should look like this:

<code>assert \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < index; (this.get(i) == \old(this.get(i)) || \old(this.get(i)) == null);</code>

This assert statement checks that for all indices `i` in the range `[0, index)`, the element at position `i` either remains the same as before the `set` operation or was initially `null`.
